        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: തട്ടിപ്പ്",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "തട്ടിപ്പ് — taṭṭippŭ — \"a fraud; a scam\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഫോണിലൂടെയുള്ള തട്ടിപ്പ് ഇപ്പോൾ കൂടുതലാണ്. phōṇilūṭeyuḷḷa taṭṭippŭ ippōḷ kūṭutalāṇŭ. Fraud over the phone is more common now."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A scam takes your money by a trick."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "തട്ടിപ്പ് (taṭṭippŭ) is native Dravidian, a noun built on തട്ടുക (taṭṭuka), \"to knock, to strike\" (DEDR 3039), which in everyday speech also means to cheat someone of money."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
